        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: شرط",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شرط — sharṭ — \"a condition\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "لي شرط واحد. lī sharṭ wāḥid. I have one condition."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: شروط, shurūṭ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شرط (sharṭ) is built on the native Arabic root sh-r-ṭ, \"to set a mark; to stipulate\" (Lane). A sharṭ is a mark set down in a bargain: a condition. شرطة, the police, is from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
